[h1]Meals at Work[/h1]
Keep crafting or researching while eating a carried meal, at 80% work speed. Prefer a lunch break? Automatic crafting breaks protect unfinished work and resume its progress after eating.

[h2]Meal delivery[/h2]
Hungry crafters can start their next workbench job and request delivery during preparation or production. Haulers deliver a suitable prepared meal directly to the worker's inventory. Orders survive short jobs and workstation departures, with a two-hour default lifetime.

[h2]Dining and compatibility[/h2]
Empty worktables can serve as dining spots. Normal tables have a distance preference; worktable distance costs twice as much by default, configurable from 1 to 5.
Eating at a workstation gives an optional -1 mood effect for one hour, respecting vanilla no-table thought nullifiers.
Supports RimWorld 1.6; requires Harmony. Includes optional Common Sense, Pick Up And Haul and Schedule Everything compatibility, and support for player mechs with an existing ordinary food need. HardworkingKz animals, Hospitality guests and fully custom work/eating drivers are not yet supported.

